"""Reader-facing current documentation, without superseded status notices."""
from pathlib import Path
from frontier import ROOT,REMAINING,FINDINGS,EVIDENCE,read,finding_path
BASE='https://sebastienpalcoux.github.io/grothendieck-ring-classification/'
def render(name,repo=ROOT):
 repo=Path(repo)
 notice='> **AI-generated research; independent human verification pending.** Exact checks establish only their stated computational scope.\n\n'
 current='**Current classification: six unresolved cases.** R8_3_1768 is excluded over the complex numbers by pivotal conjugation parity, using the established existence and complete center-domain reductions. The current continuation adds branch exclusions and conditional constructions, including the exact identification of Anyon Atlas B20-02148. No additional categorification is claimed.\n\n'
 proofs='[Current proofs and exact replay](https://github.com/sebastienpalcoux/grothendieck-ring-classification/blob/main/evidence/frontier/README.md)'
 if name=='manuscripts/README.md':
  inventory=read(repo/'data/current_manuscript_page_counts.json');rows=[]
  for r in inventory['documents']:
   if r['kind']!='mathematical_manuscript':continue
   p=Path(r['path']);href=p.relative_to('manuscripts').as_posix()if p.parts[0]=='manuscripts'else'../'+str(p)
   rows.append(f"| {r['title']} | [PDF]({href}) | [TeX]({str(Path(href).with_suffix('.tex'))}) | {r['pages']} |")
  t=inventory['totals']
  return '# Manuscripts\n\n'+current+notice+'Each current mathematical manuscript appears once, in rank order. Counts refer to based rings admitting at least one model, not to inequivalent associators.\n\n| Manuscript | PDF | Source | Pages |\n|---|---|---|---:|\n'+'\n'.join(rows)+f"\n\n**12 mathematical manuscripts, {t['mathematical_manuscript']} pages.** With the three verification guides: {t['mathematical_manuscripts_and_guides']} pages. With the current frontier report: {t['all_distinct_documents']} pages. Mirrored copies are counted once.\n\n[Current frontier report](frontier/Fusion_Ring_Frontier.pdf) · [Page inventory](../data/current_manuscript_page_counts.json) · [Publication manifest](../data/current_publication_revision.json)\n\n## Scope\n\nRanks 2–4 have unrestricted classification claims. Ranks 5–8 use explicit census bounds 20, 9, 5 and 3. Two rank-six and three rank-eight cases remain open. Rank nine through multiplicity two has 2,148 general exclusions, 76 unitary models and one unresolved case. Ranks 10–12 at multiplicity one have no unresolved cases; R12_1_623 has a complex/pseudo-unitary model with unitarity unproved.\n\n"+proofs+' · [All open cases]('+BASE+'unresolved.html)\n'
 if name=='docs/RESEARCH_STATUS.md':
  rows=[]
  for rid in REMAINING:
   text,rel=FINDINGS[rid];rows.append(f"### {rid}\n\n{text}\n\n[Proof and precise gap](../{finding_path(rid)})\n")
  return '# Current research frontier\n\n'+current+notice+proofs+'\n\n## General exclusion of R8_3_1768\n\nConjugation X tensor V tensor X* preserves the symmetry sign of a nondegenerate pivotal self-duality on V. Opposite-sign self-dual constituents must occur evenly. The exact R1768 product violates this condition. The general-complex conclusion retains the earlier sphericalization/Galois existence gate and complete center-domain theorem as explicit premises. All six required rational separation certificates replay over the complete allowed columns.\n\n[Full proof](../evidence/frontier/replay/new/r1768/PALINDROMIC_EXCLUSION.md)\n\n## Six unresolved cases\n\n'+'\n'.join(rows)+'\nNecessary-condition witnesses and candidate algebras are not counted as categorical models. [Current tensors](../data/current_remaining_cases.py) · [Atlas]('+BASE+'unresolved.html)\n'
 if name=='docs/PREPUBLICATION_REVIEW.md':
  return '# Research status and verification scope\n\n'+current+notice+'The project distinguishes proofs, their categorical premises, encoded necessary conditions, and exact computational certificates. Passing a finite relaxation does not establish a category. An exclusion applies to general complex categorification only when its reduction covers arbitrary complex fusion categories.\n\n## Current evidence\n\nThe pivotal conjugation lemma and R1768 application received two independent agent reviews. The six required rational separators were reconstructed and checked against every allowed column. The 28 current finite checks passed, including the exact Anyon Atlas comparison, nine certificates excluding the positive TY sign for R137, and an independent check of the surviving negative-sign rational witness. The separate twelve-check predecessor replay retains the R1768 exclusion and its immutable context.\n\nThe earlier general-complex existence gates and categorical completeness of the center domains remain identified mathematical inputs. Their expensive earlier searches were not regenerated in this continuation. No unitarity-only classification is transferred to an arbitrary spherical category.\n\n## Publication checks\n\nThe current manifest binds manuscript sources, compiled PDFs, website mirrors and their exact hashes. Case profiles, band totals, the six-tensor download and the complete census index are checked for consistency. The fusion-ring census itself is unchanged: 1,434,042 based rings.\n\n'+proofs+' · [Replay commands](VERIFY.md) · [Current manifests](../data/current_publication_revision.json)\n'
 if name=='docs/VERIFY.md':
  return '# Verify the current publication\n\n'+notice+'After cloning the classification repository:\n\n~~~sh\npython3 -m pip install sympy==1.14.0 numpy==2.3.5 pypdf==6.10.0\npython3 tools/restore_data.py\npython3 tools/verify_current_publication.py\npython3 tools/verify_current_publication.py --metadata-only\npython3 evidence/frontier/replay/current/run_checks.py --include-native --receipt /tmp/fusion-frontier-current.json\npython3 evidence/frontier/replay/run_checks.py\n~~~\n\nThe first command installs the verification dependencies; the second restores checksummed data. The next two validate the current ledgers, documents, website copies, profile scopes and tensors; full mode also recomputes structural ring properties. The current runner replays 28 finite checks, including the new R137 certificates and exact B20-02148 comparison. The final command separately replays twelve frozen predecessor checks, including the six complete-domain R1768 separators. Neither runner performs optimization or an associator search. Run it with ordinary Python, since some short matrix verifiers use assertions.\n\nFor runtime dependencies and the explicit inherited mathematical premises, read [the current proof index](../evidence/frontier/README.md) and [R1768 replay instructions](../evidence/frontier/replay/new/r1768/REPLAY_README.md).\n\nEarlier categorical certificates stay in their frozen rank-specific contexts. The current replay does not claim to repeat every previous exclusion or establish external hypotheses by arithmetic alone. [Manuscripts](../manuscripts/README.md) identify the corresponding proof for each rank.\n'
 if name=='docs/PROJECT_GUIDE.md':
  return '# Project guide\n\n'+current+notice+'## Read the project\n\n- [Public Atlas]('+BASE+') presents the current classification and case records.\n- [Manuscripts](../manuscripts/README.md) gives one current paper per rank or stated band.\n- [Theory and definitions]('+BASE+'theory.html) introduces fusion rings, fusion categories and the structural filters.\n- [Current research frontier](RESEARCH_STATUS.md) states exactly what remains open.\n- [Verification](VERIFY.md) provides reproducible commands and their limits.\n\n## Two complementary repositories\n\nThe [Fusion Ring Census](https://github.com/sebastienpalcoux/fusion-ring-census) enumerates based rings without a categorifiability filter. Its bounded regions contain 1,434,042 rings. This classification repository supplies categorical models and exclusions. The Atlas case directory covers the full census; detailed research profiles are supplied where available. Census-only numerical invariants are never treated as categorical models.\n\n<a id="grothendieck-rings--known-realizations-at-each-exact-multiplicity"></a>\n\n## Decisions and models\n\nAn exclusion is recorded at its proved scope: general complex, pivotal, spherical, pseudo-unitary or unitary. A restriction at one level is not automatically an exclusion at a broader level. A realized based ring has at least one categorical model; inequivalent associators are not counted separately. R12_1_623 is recorded as complex/pseudo-unitary with unitarity unproved.\n\nA model must be categorically constructed and matched to the full tensor by an exact based isomorphism. Matching FP dimensions or modular spectra is insufficient. Necessary center matrices, rational witnesses and conditional algebra constructions retain unresolved status.\n\n## Current data\n\n[All-rank classification totals](../data/classification_summary_all_ranks.csv) · [Current publication manifest](../data/current_publication_revision.json) · [Six open tensors](../data/current_remaining_cases.py) · '+proofs+'\n\n## Construction catalogue\n\n“New” refers only to a specific construction that has not, to our knowledge, been explicitly recorded in the literature. The constructions use known methods, with hypotheses and fusion rules checked in the project; this is not a claim of novelty up to tensor equivalence or of exoticness. Independent human verification remains pending. [New constructions]('+BASE+'constructions.html).\n'
 return None

